course: dictionary
lesson: 15506
title: Powerful words: subjugate
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words are formal, so you meet them in history books, news reports and serious talk. Subjugate is one of them. Read the words around it, and the clues will tell you what it means.
explain: «The king sent soldiers to subjugate the villages, and soon everyone had to obey him.» The words everyone had to obey tell you that subjugate means to defeat people and take control of them.
explain: The word can also be used in a gentler way: «Lena chose to subjugate her wish for ice cream to the needs of her team.» Here it means putting something less important under something more important. Try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have got it.
fact: Subjugate is a formal verb. Its forms are subjugate, subjugates, subjugated and subjugating.
fact: «Subjugate» means to defeat people or a country and take control of them so they must obey, often taking away their freedom.
fact: «Subjugate» can also mean to make something less important than something else.
fact: History lessons use this word when they talk about empires that subjugated other peoples, and about how those peoples were treated unfairly.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «subjugated peoples» and «subjugate a nation».
exercise: «The strong empire tried to subjugate the smaller nation.» What does subjugate mean here? | Make friends with the nation | *Defeat the nation and take control so it must obey | Move the nation to a new place | Give the nation a gift
exercise: «Sam chose to subjugate his wish to watch TV to the needs of his family.» What does subjugate mean here? | Forget that it exists | Make it bigger than before | *Make it less important than the family's needs | Shout about it to everyone
exercise: Which phrase describes people who have been defeated and forced to obey? | Quiet school library | *Subjugated peoples | Bright summer picnic | Shiny new bicycles
test: Ella reads, «The rebels refused to be subjugated.» What does subjugated mean? | Turned into a famous story | Ignored by everyone around them | Given a prize for bravery | *Defeated and forced to obey
test: «Mia had to subjugate her own plans to help her team.» What happened to Mia's plans? | Her plans were forced on the whole team | *Her plans became less important than the team's | Her plans were written down and shared | Her plans grew bigger than the team's
exam: Which sentence uses subjugate in the sense of taking control of people by force? | *The invaders tried to subjugate the island and make its people obey | The young artist decided to subjugate the paint colours | The baker began to subjugate the dough | The class chose to subjugate their wishes to the team
